{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:b4e1fb149ce79d22","name":"Militia Saboteur","source":{"id":"source:reference-b4e1fb149ce79d22","title":"Militia Saboteur","revision":25260,"timestamp":"2024-11-13T20:27:54Z","sha256":"67bd798c49c3e0aa32f554528a2448ffc24f00e55c3613c12f6794ba1ee2b0b6","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=25260","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Militia%20Saboteur&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-b4e1fb149ce79d22","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Force Unleashed Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Unleashed_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Affiliations: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Kota's Militia"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Kota%27s_Militia","referenceId":"reference:7f120847ffcfac7c"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Galactic Republic"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Galactic_Republic","referenceId":"reference:332055cafc4223eb"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Rebel Alliance"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Rebel_Alliance","referenceId":"reference:52c543ff6d31425c"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The men and women serving in ",{"tag":"a","children":["Kota's Militia"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Kota%27s_Militia","referenceId":"reference:7f120847ffcfac7c"}," represent an enlightened class of citizens who realize that their civic obligation to the Republic requires their direct involvement in galactic affairs. Despite their varied origins- military academy graduates, ",{"tag":"a","children":["CorSec"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/CorSec","referenceId":"reference:b33aae470a5aee7e"}," agents, responsible nobles- they all believe the burden of military service shouldn't fall to an army of clones that have no vested interest in the Republic, but to the very people who stand to benefit from victory.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["These citizens volunteer when ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Clone Wars"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Clone_Wars"}," begin, drawn to Master ",{"tag":"a","children":["Rahm Kota"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Rahm_Kota","referenceId":"reference:f59570f543b5d020"}," because he is one of the few generals leading nonclone forces. They undergo military training under his tutelage, including small-unit tactics and commando operations. The militia undertakes several special assignments and joins other nonclone units such as ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Antarian Rangers"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Antarian_Rangers","referenceId":"reference:b1e2fba2947ee070"}," for larger assaults. Like many of those units, they fall victim to Order 66 and share the same fate as their Jedi commanders: to become hunted outlaws labeled as traitors to ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Galactic Empire"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Galactic_Empire","referenceId":"reference:f9c9a48674cc3415"},".\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["During ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Dark Times"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Dark_Times"},", the militia rallies around Master ",{"tag":"a","children":["Rahm Kota"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Rahm_Kota","referenceId":"reference:f59570f543b5d020"},". The soldiers spend their time ensuring their safety, seeking new havens, establishing bases and contacts, working with allies, obtaining necessary supplies and transport, and staying one step ahead of Vader's agents. Once they stabilize their position, the militia members turn to Master Kota for inspiration in striking back at nearby Imperial installations in ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Outer Rim"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Outer_Rim?action=edit&redlink=1"},". Most become casualties in these small assaults; they ultimately fall victim to the agents sent by Vader to hunt them down.\n"]},"\n\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Mil